<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajaraja Narendra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1022–1061</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajaraja Narendra was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-chalukyas">Eastern Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vengi">Vengi</a> in Andhra, closely allied by marriage with the Chola dynasty. He ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajahmundry">Rajamahendravaram</a> (Rajahmundry), and under his patronage the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nannaya">Nannaya</a> began the Telugu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, the founding work of Telugu literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaraja-narendra.jpg" alt="Rajaraja Narendra" width="320" height="520" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chakravarthi999 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Rajaraja_Narendra_founder_of_rajahmundry_city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
